course: dictionary
lesson: 12143
title: Squeezed tight: compaction
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Compaction means pressing something together so it becomes tighter and smaller, with less space inside it. Think of squeezing a sponge: the air comes out and it gets smaller. «The rubbish truck used compaction to squeeze the bags into a small space.» The bags are pressed flat, so there is less space in the truck.
explain: In science, compaction is the squeezing of layers of sediment or soil by the weight on top of them. Sediment is tiny bits of mud and sand that settle in layers. «Over millions of years, the weight of new layers caused compaction in the mud at the bottom of the lake.» As the layers press down, the mud gets tighter and can slowly turn into rock.
explain: Compaction is a clue word that tells you things are being pressed tighter. Look at the words around it. Words like heavy, weight, squeeze or pressed often sit close by. Try your meaning in the sentence: if «pressed tighter» fits, you have it.
fact: Compaction means pressing something together so it becomes tighter and smaller.
fact: In science, compaction squeezes layers of sediment or soil under the weight on top.
fact: Compaction, with cementation, helps turn layers of sediment into sedimentary rock.
fact: «Soil compaction» from heavy machines or feet makes it hard for roots and water to get in.
fact: Compaction is uncountable, so you say «some compaction», not «a compaction».
exercise: «The rubbish truck used compaction to squeeze the bags into a small space.» What does compaction mean here? | Washing the rubbish clean | Adding more rubbish to make the truck bigger | *Pressing things tighter so they take up less space | Spreading the rubbish out wide
exercise: «Heavy tractors caused soil compaction, so the water could not sink into the field.» Why could the water not get in? | The water was too cold | *The soil was pressed so tight there was less space for it | The soil was full of stones | The soil was too dry and cracked
exercise: Layers of mud pile up at the bottom of a lake for millions of years. Which process slowly squeezes them into rock? | Evaporation | Erosion | Melting | *Compaction
test: «Over millions of years, the weight of layers above caused compaction of the sand.» What does this sentence tell you? | The sand was washed away by a river | The sand was blown into the sea | *The sand was pressed tighter and harder | The sand was heated until it turned to glass
test: Which of these is an example of compaction? | *Stamping down wet snow to make a hard, tight path | Pouring water into a glass | Blowing up a balloon | Spreading jam on bread
exam: Which sentence uses compaction correctly? | «The compaction of the birds sang loudly in the trees.» | *«The compaction of the wet sand made it dense and hard.» | «The compaction of the sky was bright blue.» | «The compaction of the children ran to school.»
